# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/500 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 18 deg Earth-central angle (2141 km away, zenith 113.2 deg,
# azimuth 270 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 4.4e+05 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 1.15 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 43.74 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_DISTPAR0036
R2_DISTPAR0036.ParticleType 1
R2_DISTPAR0036.Beam FarFieldGaussian 111.398 124.686 4.014
R2_DISTPAR0036.Spectrum File R2_DISTPAR0036_spectrum.dat
R2_DISTPAR0036.Flux 0.318828
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835968035.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): R2_DISTPAR0036_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R2_DISTPAR0036.Lightcurve File false R2_DISTPAR0036_lightcurve_shifted.dat
R2_DISTPAR0036.EarthOccultation false
